    {
      "id": "sol.amc-8-2013-p15.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Subtract the known number from each equation: \\[3^p=90-81=9,\\] \\[2^r=76-44=32,\\] \\[6^s=1421-125=1296.\\]\n\nTherefore \\(p=2\\), \\(r=5\\), and \\(s=4\\). Their product is \\(2\\cdot5\\cdot4=40\\).\n\nThus, B is the correct answer.",
